#: includes/openid-connect-generic-role-mapping.php:445
msgid "Assign WordPress roles based on the roles of a user in Hitobito. The role is updated on every login with Hitobito. Administrators are never changed, and no rule can grant administrator access."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is the name of the Hitobito scope.
#: includes/openid-connect-generic-role-mapping.php:449
#, php-format
msgid "The mapping requests the additional scope %s. It has to be enabled for the OAuth application in Hitobito before you enable the mapping, otherwise the login fails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/openid-connect-generic-role-mapping.php:486
msgid "One rule per line: group ids | role classes | WordPress role. Separate several group ids or role classes with commas, * matches everything (e.g. Group::Abteilung::*). The rules are checked from top to bottom and the first matching rule wins, so put the rules with more rights first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/openid-connect-generic-role-mapping.php:489
msgid "Hitobito only reports the group a role is directly in. To match a whole department, list the department and all of its subgroups. Each user profile shows the Hitobito roles of the last login, including the group ids and role classes."
msgstr ""

